  "description": "An open library of ~199 life-science and bioinformatics 'skills' — plain-markdown SKILL.md files that give AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, Windsurf) procedural domain knowledge across RNA-seq, single-cell, genomics, proteomics, drug discovery, cheminformatics, biostatistics, structural/systems biology, and lab automation. Skills are grouped as toolkits, database connectors, guides, and pipelines; they are read directly by the agent with no runtime dependencies (Python 3.12+ is used only for validation scripts, and each skill lists its own tool prerequisites). The project reports 92.0% accuracy on BixBench-Verified-50 versus a 65.3% Claude Code (Opus 4.6) baseline — a self-reported figure, not independently verified. It powers the OmicsHorizon web platform (omicshorizon.ai).",
